  "hypothesis": "Geothermal-conduit off-catalogue hypothesis: blind/young geothermal faults missing from the USGS+INGENIOUS catalogue carry a joint signature of dilatation (geod_dilaterate>0), curvature/edge (tc above median), conductivity (cond_surf above median), gravity gradient magnitude, and proximity to historic seismicity (small deq_n100a15). Dots are placed only in novel geothermal territory outside the catalogue buffer and outside all nine focus-site registry halos.",
  "mechanism": "Five training bands are rank-blended (geometric mean, weights 0.25/0.25/0.20/0.15/0.15) so a cell scores high only when the independent fields agree \u2014 suppressing single-field mimics. The surface is masked to pixels >3 px from catalogue faults and >3 px from every focus-site raster dot. Greedy NMS (4 px separation) emits ~20k dots on the surviving ridges.",
